_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaJeztah/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaJeztah/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaJeztah/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaJeztah/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaJeztah/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaJeztah/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaJeztah/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaJeztah/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaJeztah/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-03-23T11:09:32Z","updated_at":"2023-03-23T11:09:32Z","body":"From your last comment, I suspect this may be related to the kernel; a quick search brought me to https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/1e579caa18b96f9eb18f4f5416658cd15f37c062, which namespaced this sysctl, and (if GitHub shows it correctly) that change was part of kernel 4.6-rc1 and up (from https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blame/fff5a5e7f528b2ed2c335991399a766c2cf01103/Documentation/networking/ip-sysctl.rst#L438, it looks like the sysctl itself was part of kernel 2.6 already, but not namespaced).\r\n\r\nRedHat's (CentOS) kernels are known to have back ported various features though, so not sure if that change was back ported by them.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/docker/cli/issues/comments/1480998115/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"thaJeztah","id":1804568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDQ1Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1804568?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaJeztah","html_url":"https://github.com/thaJeztah","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thaJezt